      "html" : "<\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-194108\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-194108\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div>Ducts used to convey hazardous exhaust shall be constructed of materials approved for installation in such an exhaust system and shall comply with one of the following:<\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-194109\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-194109\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div>&#160;&#160;&#160;1.&#160;&#160;&#160;Ducts shall be constructed of approved G90 galvanized sheet steel, with a minimum nominal thickness as specified in <Link class=\"Jump\" to=\"{{ pathname: '\/codes\/newyorkcity\/latest\/NYCadmin\/0-0-0-194107', hash: '#JD_MCTable510.9' }}\">Table 510.9<\/Link>.<\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-194110\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-194110\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div>&#160;&#160;&#160;2.&#160;&#160;&#160;Ducts used in systems exhausting nonflammable corrosive fumes or vapors shall be constructed of nonmetallic materials that exhibit a flame spread index of 25 or less and a smoke-developed index of 50 or less when tested in accordance with ASTM E 84 or UL 723 and that are listed and labeled the application.<\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-194111\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-194111\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div>Where the products being exhausted are detrimental to the duct material, the ducts shall be constructed of alternative materials that are compatible with the exhaust.<\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-194112\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-194112\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div><a name=\"JD_MCTable510.9\" id=\"JD_MCTable510.9\" title=\"MC Table 510.9\"><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: bold;font-style: normal;text-decoration:none;display: inline;\">Table 510.9<br><\/br>Minimum Duct Thickness<\/span><\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-194113\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-194113\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div style=\"margin-bottom=10pt\">&#160;<div class=\"xsl-table\">",
      "id" : "23478-html-1",
      "kind" : "html",
      "plainText" : "Ducts used to convey hazardous exhaust shall be constructed of materials approved for installation in such an exhaust system and shall comply with one of the following:\n\n 1. Ducts shall be constructed of approved G90 galvanized sheet steel, with a minimum nominal thickness as specified in Table 510.9 .\n\n 2. Ducts used in systems exhausting nonflammable corrosive fumes or vapors shall be constructed of nonmetallic materials that exhibit a flame spread index of 25 or less and a smoke-developed index of 50 or less when tested in accordance with ASTM E 84 or UL 723 and that are listed and labeled the application.\n\n Where the products being exhausted are detrimental to the duct material, the ducts shall be constructed of alternative materials that are compatible with the exhaust.\n\n Table 510.9\n Minimum Duct Thickness"
    },
    {
